 "text": "Hi, how are you holding out? It's genuinely considerate of you to let them know. Many weddings move around food because of this, and small box of little items for you to eat is reasonable. Then ask if there's a big piece of cake you can have a piece of, or if there's a burger bar. Many places have an allergy friendly option. No worries. Was that something you needed to ask about the wedding, or something else? Weddings tend to pull at all kinds of emotions. Is there anything specific you'd like to chat about? Offer to bring something if they' short on guests, but check with them first, just in case someone else is bringing it. You don't have to. Just offer, and be there for them if their day gets larger than they expected.",
